  <iati-identifier>47045-UGA-S-MoFPED-1</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the health and community systems for quality, equitable and timely service delivery - Uganda (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda, RSSH, Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development of the Republic of Uganda (MoFPED)This program has the following goals: To strengthen the health and commodity systems for quality, equitable and timely service delivery. The objectives of this program are: Build capacity to reform social and cultural discriminatory practices against vulnerable groups.  Expand storage capacity at National Medical Stores and Joint Medical Stores.  Strengthen collaboration, referral and linkages among community level actors.  Strengthen community level legal literacy and access to legal aid.  Strengthen inventory management capacity at national and facility level.  Strengthen National and facility level quantification and procurement planning.  Strengthen procurement and supply management capacity at national and sub national levels to be able to sustain the national response to HIV, TB and Malaria.  Strengthen the MOH monitoring and evaluation to enable evidence based decision making, sector learning and performance improvement.  Strengthen the national health information and M&amp;E systems for evidence based decision making for HIV, TB and Malaria response in Uganda.  Strengthen the national health information and M&amp;E systems for evidence based decision making for HIV, TB and Malaria response in Uganda.  Strengthen the organization and management of the national health information system to provide complete, accurate and timely information.  Strengthen the quality assurance systems at the National Drug Authority.  To attain community empowerment to respond to the health needs and ensure social accountability and inclusiveness to achieve desired health outcomes in Uganda</narrative>
  </description>
